<p>
I've been studying French since November 2025 because I want to help my daughter learn it. After about eight months of taking pronunciation tutoring sessions once or twice a week and writing my journal in French, I decided to try conversation-focused tutoring sessions in June 2026. These sessions help me get used to talking and identify the gaps in my active vocabulary.
</p>

<p>
These tutoring conversations feel quite different from other conversations I have.
In real-life conversations with my husband and daughter, we usually leave a lot of space between sentences. When I'm hanging out with other people, I prefer to listen more than I talk. Tutoring sessions are different. I am investing time and money in practising talking. I can get a lot of listening practice from YouTube, so it's less about listening to people, although I still want to practice asking follow-up questions and connecting what the tutor says with my personal experiences.
</p>

<p>
In those conversation classes with French tutors, I want to get a
sense of how much I'm actually talking. I was motivated to visualize
this after some sessions with a tutor who tended to go into lecture
mode. I found myself needing to be a bit firmer about directing the
conversation instead of slipping into a more passive role.
</p>

<p>
I use OBS to record my sessions (with the tutor's permission, of course). I've configured it so that <a href="https://obsproject.com/kb/multiple-audio-track-recording-guide">my microphone goes on one track</a> and my computer audio goes on another track, which makes it easy to analyze my side of the conversation without needing to use speaker diarization.
</p>

<p>
I used <a href="https://gemini.google.com">Google Gemini</a> to generate a script that uses <a href="https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad">Silero voice activity detection</a> to analyze my side of the multi-track MKV recording.
</p>

<p>
Here's the file it generated. <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/2026/10/visualizing-the-balance-of-speaking-in-my-french-conversations-with-tutors/vad-file.py">file:///home/sacha/proj/speech/vad-file.py</a>
</p>

<p>
I call it with:
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh"><code><span class="org-keyword">for</span> FILE<span class="org-keyword"> in</span> ~/recordings/*conversation*.mkv; <span class="org-keyword">do if</span> [ <span class="org-negation-char">!</span> -f <span class="org-string">"$FILE-vad.txt"</span> ]; <span class="org-keyword">then</span> python vad-file.py -f <span class="org-string">"$FILE"</span> -t 2 sacha 3 tutor -s 500 -o <span class="org-string">"$FILE-vad.txt"</span>; <span class="org-keyword">fi</span>; <span class="org-keyword">done</span>
</code></pre>
</div>


